`tests/packs-suggest.test.ts` covers `searchSkillsSh` and `packsAdd`, but the new PR-URL branch added here has real, untested logic living inline in the commander action: detecting a URL argument, filtering dependency names out of `stack.tags` so the API isn't spammed, the `slice(0, 8)` cap, and the `exit(1)` when no tags are detected. Because it sits inside `.action()` in `src/cli.ts`, no unit test can reach it — the tag-derivation rule can silently break (e.g. every dependency leaking into the query, or the empty-tags error path never firing) and the 327-test suite stays green.

